       If  the  output  string would exceed _m_a_x bytes, _e_r_r_n_o is _n_o_t set.  This
       makes it impossible to distinguish this error case from cases where the
       _f_o_r_m_a_t  string  legitimately  produces  a  zero‐length  output  string.
       POSIX.1‐2001 does _n_o_t specify any _e_r_r_n_o settings for ssttrrffttiimmee().

       Some  buggy  versions  of ggcccc(1) complain about the use of %%cc: _w_a_r_n_i_n_g_:
       _`_%_c_' _y_i_e_l_d_s _o_n_l_y _l_a_s_t _2 _d_i_g_i_t_s _o_f _y_e_a_r  _i_n  _s_o_m_e  _l_o_c_a_l_e_s.   Of  course
